hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  SAR receives {duress_placeholder, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, \n approved_withdrawal_id} from WT. It decrypts duress_placeholder using the Boomlet-to-SAR CBC/CMAC envelope \n context and sar_privkey to get duress_placeholder_plaintext. It classifies the plaintext as valid safe if it is all-zero \n 32-byte padding, valid duress if its derived doxing_data_identifier exists, \n or malformed otherwise. If it was valid duress and the tuple of approved_withdrawal_id, the received \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, and envelope IV of duress_placeholder was not previously saved, \n SAR activates duress response, uses duress_placeholder_plaintext as doxing_key_for_sar to decrypt \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar, derives device_data_key from doxing_key_for_sar for each retained upload, \n derives dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys from device_data_key, \n decrypts each retained upload's dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_device_data_key with \n dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys, and makes every retained upload available to SEARCH AND RESCUE. \n For valid safe or duress placeholders, SAR signs duress_placeholder with sar_privkey and encrypts it with \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. Malformed placeholders are rejected before any acknowledgment is created.
