hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt from Niso (and \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt from Peers). WT handles exact ping retries under SPEC Section 15.7 before processing new pings. If this \n is the first ping received, WT \n initializes reached_pings_collection with an empty set and goes into a loop that ends when \n reached_pings_collection[peer_i_id] has a valid value \n for every peer. WT decrypts peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i and verifies \n boomlet_i_identity_pubkey's signature. Wt then \n separates duress_placeholder, which is the padding, and peer_i_ping. This diagram expands only peer 0's SAR \n path: WT sends peer 0's duress_placeholder and \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey to peer 0's SAR. Other peers' placeholders are routed to their own setup-bound SARs \n in the corresponding peer flows.
hnote over WT #Pink:  Handle exact ping retries under SPEC 15.7; return after receipt-only delivery.
note over WT #Lavender:  if for peer_i_id in peer_ids reached_pings_collection[peer_i_id] exists: \n break PING_PONG_LOOP.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i := decrypt_from_boomlet_i(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_ping", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt)
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping_envelope", \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded := \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i.content \n duress_placeholder := peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded.padding \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i := peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded.content

' Step 48
WT o-> SAR:  <b>WithdrawalWtSarMessage2 \n duress_placeholder \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n approved_withdrawal_id
hnote over WT, SAR #LightYellow:  Expanded path for peer 0 only. For peer i, WT sends peer_i's \n duress_placeholder with boomlet_i_identity_pubkey to peer i's selected SAR.
hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  SAR receives {duress_placeholder, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, \n approved_withdrawal_id} from WT. It decrypts duress_placeholder using the Boomlet-to-SAR CBC/CMAC envelope \n context and sar_privkey to get duress_placeholder_plaintext. It classifies the plaintext as valid safe if it is all-zero \n 32-byte padding, valid duress if its derived doxing_data_identifier exists, \n or malformed otherwise. If it was valid duress and the tuple of approved_withdrawal_id, the received \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, and envelope IV of duress_placeholder was not previously saved, \n SAR activates duress response, uses duress_placeholder_plaintext as doxing_key_for_sar to decrypt \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar, derives device_data_key from doxing_key_for_sar for each retained upload, \n derives dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys from device_data_key, \n decrypts each retained upload's dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_device_data_key with \n dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys, and makes every retained upload available to SEARCH AND RESCUE. \n For valid safe or duress placeholders, SAR signs duress_placeholder with sar_privkey and encrypts it with \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. Malformed placeholders are rejected before any acknowledgment is created.
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  duress_placeholder_plaintext := decrypt_from_boomlet_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: duress_placeholder)
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  is_safe_placeholder := (duress_placeholder_plaintext == zero_bytes_32) \n derived_doxing_data_identifier := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", \n duress_placeholder_plaintext) \n is_valid_duress_placeholder := (!is_safe_placeholder && sar_record_exists(derived_doxing_data_identifier))
hnote over SAR #Pink:  Assert is_safe_placeholder || is_valid_duress_placeholder
opt #LightBlue SEARCH AND RESCUE [is_valid_duress_placeholder and (approved_withdrawal_id, \n boomlet_identity_pubkey, duress_placeholder.iv) not previously saved]
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  doxing_data_identifier := derived_doxing_data_identifier \n doxing_key_for_sar := duress_placeholder_plaintext \n static_doxing_data := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: derive_cbc_cmac_keys(doxing_key_for_sar, \n "Boomerang/sar_stored_data"), context: canonical_encode("Boomerang", PROTOCOL_VERSION, "sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier), envelope: \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar) \n retained_dynamic_doxing_data_uploads := all_retained_uploads(doxing_data_identifier) \n dynamic_doxing_data_history := [] \n for each retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload in retained_dynamic_doxing_data_uploads: \n   device_data_key := kdf_counter_cmac_aes256(doxing_key_for_sar, \n   "Boomerang/sar_dynamic_device_data_key/v1", \n   canonical_encode(retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.device_id), 32) \n   dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys := derive_cbc_cmac_keys(device_data_key, "Boomerang/sar_stored_data") \n   dynamic_doxing_data := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys, \n   context: canonical_encode("Boomerang", PROTOCOL_VERSION, "sar_dynamic_data", doxing_data_identifier, \n   retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.device_id, retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.upload_id, \n   retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.upload_seq_num), \n   envelope: retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_device_data_key) \n   dynamic_doxing_data_history.append(dynamic_doxing_data) \n end for \n save(approved_withdrawal_id, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, duress_placeholder.iv) \n Enter SEARCH_AND_RESCUE_MODE
end
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar := sign_message(sar_privkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/sar_placeholder_response", duress_placeholder) \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0 := encrypt_for_boomlet_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_sar_placeholder_response", approved_withdrawal_id), \n content: duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar)

' Step 49
SAR o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalSarWtMessage2 \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0 \n from SAR and continues processing peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0 and peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i. \n It verifies boomlet_i_identity_pubkey's signature on peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i and checks \n approved_withdrawal_id to be the one expected. If this is not the first ping it also checks that ping_seq_num \n has increased.  If reached_mystery_flag is 1, WT assigns \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i to reached_pings_collection[peer_i_id]. WT constructs pong containing \n approved_withdrawal_id, most_work_bitcoin_block_height, \n and Collection<peer_j_ping_signed_by_boomlet_j> [for each Peer i's pong include \n peer_j_ping_signed_by_boomlet_j of all other peers \n (i != j)], if it isn't the first pong composed WT waits for at least 1 block to pass. WT signs the pong and \n encrypts it for Boomlet to get pong_i_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_i. \n It then sends pong_0_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_0 alongside \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0 \n to Niso and pong_i_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_i [1 <= i <= 4] to other peers.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  most_work_bitcoin_block_height := rpc_client.get_block_height()
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", \n peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_i_ping := peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i.content
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert peer_i_ping.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id.
hnote over WT #Pink:  If not the first ping received from peer_i: \n Assert peer_i_ping.ping_seq_num has increased.
hnote over WT #Pink:  If the first ping received from peer_i: \n Assert peer_i_ping.reached_mystery_flag != 1.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  if peer_i_ping.reached_mystery_flag == 1: \n reached_pings_collection[peer_i_id] := peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i
hnote over WT #Pink:  If not the first pong: \n Assert most_work_bitcoin_block_height >= (pong.event_block_height + \n REQUIRED_MINIMUM_DISTANCE_IN_BLOCKS_BETWEEN_PING_AND_PONG)  [wait until a block has passed since the last sent \n pong]
hnote over WT #Lavender:  prev_pings_i := ordered Collection<peer_j_ping_signed_by_boomlet_j> by \n peer_ids_collection where j != i \n pong_i := Pong{ \n approved_withdrawal_id: approved_withdrawal_id \n event_block_height := most_work_bitcoin_block_height \n prev_pings: prev_pings_i \n } \n pong_i_signed_by_wt := sign_message(wt_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/pong", pong_i) \n pong_i_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_i := encrypt_for_boomlet_i(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_pong", approved_withdrawal_id), \n content: pong_i_signed_by_wt)

