' Step 51
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage6 \n pong_0_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_0 \n niso_0_event_block_height \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {pong_0_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_0, \n niso_0_event_block_height, duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0} \n from Niso. It first decrypts duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0, verifies \n sar_pubkey's signature on \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar and checks to see if the content matches of the duress_placeholder that it \n had sent to WT. It then decrypts \n pong_0_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_0 to get pong_0_signed_by_wt and verifies wt_pubkey's \n signature. Boomlet then checks approved_withdrawal_id to match the expected value and pong to be fresh \n according to niso_0_event_block_height. It then takes out \n prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i from pong_0 for every other peer i, verifies boomlet_i_identity_pubkey's \n signature, checks approved_withdrawal_id is the one expected, if it's not the first ping received the \n ping_seq_num has increased, if \n reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] was previously assigned a value reached_mystery_flag is not 0. Boomlet performs any requested consent rotation. \n Otherwise Boomlet draws an unbiased \n duress_check_draw := random_integer(1, DURESS_CHECK_INTERVAL_IN_BLOCKS). If duress_check_draw == 1, Boomlet \n enters into a duress_check to update duress_placeholder_plaintext. \n Otherwise it keeps the current duress_placeholder_plaintext, but the next ping still uses a freshly encrypted \n duress_placeholder.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar := decrypt_from_sar(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_sar_placeholder_response", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(sar_pubkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/sar_placeholder_response", duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar.content == duress_placeholder
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  pong_0_signed_by_wt := decrypt_from_wt(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_pong", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: pong_0_signed_by_wt_encrypted_by_wt_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(wt_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/pong", \n pong_0_signed_by_wt) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  pong_0 := pong_0_signed_by_wt.content \n prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i := pong_0.prev_pings[i] [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert pong_0.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert pong_0.event_block_height >= (niso_0_event_block_height - \n TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PONG_BY_WT_TO_REVIEWING_THE_PONG_IN_PEERS_BOOMLET) \n Assert pong_0.event_block_height <= niso_0_event_block_height
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert count(pong_0.prev_pings) == (count(peer_ids_collection) - 1) \n Assert pong_0.prev_pings contains exactly one signed ping for each \n peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey [1 <= i <= 4] \n Assert pong_0.prev_pings contains no ping signed by boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n Assert pong_0.prev_pings has no duplicate signers and no missing non-recipient peers \n Assert pong_0.prev_pings is ordered by peer_ids_collection with peer_ids_collection[0] omitted
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_i_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", \n prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  prev_ping_i := prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert prev_ping_i.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n if not the first ping received from peer_i Assert that peer_i_ping.ping_seq_num has increased. [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  If reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] != Null \n Assert prev_ping_i.reached_mystery_flag != 0
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender: Boomlet performs any requested consent rotation.
group duress_check [ if resuming after consent rotation or random_integer(1, DURESS_CHECK_INTERVAL_IN_BLOCKS) == 1]:
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_check_space := DuressCheckSpace{space: random_permutation([1..193])} \n duress_check_nonce := random_bytes(32) \n duress_check_space_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{ \n content: duress_check_space \n nonce: duress_check_nonce } \n store outstanding {duress_check_nonce, duress_check_space, phase} \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st := encrypt_for_st_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_challenge"), \n content: duress_check_space_with_nonce)

' Step 52
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage6 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st \n from Boomlet and forwards it to ST.

' Step 53
Niso o-> ST:  <b>WithdrawalNisoStMessage3 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from \n Niso, decrypts it to get duress_check_space_with_nonce, \n maps each integer in duress_check_space through DURESS_DISPLAY_VOCABULARY, creates 5 independently shuffled \n display columns from the single list, \n and keeps display-to-original-index mappings locally.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_check_space_with_nonce := decrypt_from_boomlet_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_challenge"), \n envelope: duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st) \n duress_check_space := duress_check_space_with_nonce.content \n duress_display_columns := independently_shuffle_with_index_maps(duress_check_space.space, columns: 5)

' Step 54
ST o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalStOutput3 \n duress_display_columns
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives 5 independently shuffled columns from ST. If he is not being \n coerced he will select 1 country in each column to replicate the duress_consent_set \n and inputs it to ST.
hnote over User #Lavender:  user_selection := select_one_from_each(duress_display_columns)

' Step 55
User o-> ST:  <b>WithdrawalStInput3 \n user_selection
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives the displayed selections from User, converts them into indices in \n Boomlet's original single list, then creates \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce using the nonce from previously received duress_check_space_with_nonce, \n encrypts it for Boomlet and sends it to Niso.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_signal_index := \n original_indices_from_display_selection(duress_display_columns, user_selection) \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{ \n content: duress_signal_index \n nonce: duress_check_space_with_nonce.nonce } \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 := encrypt_for_boomlet_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_response"), \n content: duress_signal_index_with_nonce)

' Step 56
ST o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalStNisoMessage3 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 \n from ST and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 57
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage7 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Niso. Boomlet rejects no outstanding duress \n check, wrong phase, duplicate response, \n wrong nonce, wrong count, duplicate indices, or out-of-range indices. If valid, Boomlet resolves the returned \n original-list indices against \n the single list in duress_check_space assigning the resulting integers to duress_signal. \n Boomlet consumes the answer and updates under_duress := under_duress OR (duress_signal != duress_consent_set). \n The placeholder plaintext is doxing_key_for_sar while the `under_duress` flag is true and zero_bytes_32 otherwise. \n duress_placeholder_plaintext is updated; the next ping re-encrypts the current plaintext after this optional \n check.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_signal_index_with_nonce := decrypt_from_st_0(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_response"), \n envelope: duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert outstanding duress check exists for current phase \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.nonce == duress_check_nonce \n Assert count(duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices) == 5 \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are distinct \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are in range [1..193]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  consume outstanding duress check \n duress_signal := duress_check_space.space[duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices] \n doxing_key_for_sar := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes) \n under_duress := under_duress | (duress_signal != duress_consent_set) \n duress_placeholder_plaintext := Evaluate(under_duress, doxing_key_for_sar) [either \n all-zero 32-byte padding or doxing_key_for_sar]
end group
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Regardless of whether a new duress procedure ran, Boomlet freshly encrypts \n duress_placeholder_plaintext for SAR. \n Counter advancement is evaluated before updating last_seen_block and \n occurs only if the local chain view advanced and every other peer's prev_ping_i.last_seen_block is within the \n accepted boundary around the current local Niso block height. Independently of counter advancement, every otherwise \n valid pong then updates last_seen_block by at most \n JUMP_IN_BLOCKS_IF_LAST_SEEN_BLOCK_LAGS_BEHIND_NISO_EVENT_BLOCK_HEIGHT_IN_BOOMLET toward \n niso_0_event_block_height. It records monotonic reached flags and sets its own reached_mystery_flag \n once counter reaches mystery, then generates a fresh ping with incremented ping_seq_num.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_placeholder := encrypt_for_sar(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder", approved_withdrawal_id), \n content: duress_placeholder_plaintext)
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  counter_advance_allowed := niso_0_event_block_height > last_seen_block \n && forall peer_i [1 <= i <= 4]: prev_ping_i.last_seen_block >= (niso_0_event_block_height - \n TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_CREATING_PING_BY_OTHER_PEERS_TO_REVIEWING_THE_PING_IN_PEER_BOOMLET) && \n prev_ping_i.last_seen_block <= niso_0_event_block_height
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  if reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] == Null and \n prev_ping_i.reached_mystery_flag==1: \n reached_boomlets_collection[peer_i_id] := prev_ping_i_signed_by_boomlet_i
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  if counter_advance_allowed: counter += 1 \n if last_seen_block < niso_0_event_block_height: \n last_seen_block := min(niso_0_event_block_height, (last_seen_block + \n JUMP_IN_BLOCKS_IF_LAST_SEEN_BLOCK_LAGS_BEHIND_NISO_EVENT_BLOCK_HEIGHT_IN_BOOMLET))
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  if counter >= mystery: \n reached_mystery_flag := 1
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  _peer_0_ping := Ping{ \n approved_withdrawal_id: approved_withdrawal_id, \n last_seen_block: last_seen_block \n ping_seq_num: (ping_seq_num += 1) \n reached_mystery_flag: reached_mystery_flag} \n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", \n _peer_0_ping) \n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded := PaddedMessage{ \n content: _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0, \n padding: duress_placeholder \n } \n _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping_envelope", _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded) \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt := \n encrypt_for_wt(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_ping", approved_withdrawal_id), \n content: _peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0)
end

' Step 58
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage7 \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt from Boomlet and \n forwards it to WT.

' Step 59
Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage4 \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt
autonumber 59 "<b>[00]"

' Step 59 - b
Peers o-> WT:  peer_i_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i_padded_signed_by_boomlet_i_encrypted_by_boomlet_i_for_wt [1 <= \n i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives \n peer_0_ping_signed_by_boomlet_0_padded_signed_by_boomlet_0_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_wt from Niso and jumps \n back to the beginning \n of the PING_PONG_LOOP. if the loop breaks WT sends its reached_pings_collection to all Peers.
end
group Transaction Finalization and Relay

' Step 60
WT o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage4 \n reached_pings_collection
autonumber 60 "<b>[00]"

' Step 60 - b
WT o-> Peers:  <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage4 \n reached_pings_collection
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives reached_pings_collection from WT. It verifies that the \n collection contains exactly one current reached ping from every peer, in setup peer order, with \n valid signatures, \n expected approved_withdrawal_id, current ping sequence, fresh last_seen_block, and reached_mystery_flag set. \n Only after those checks does Niso hydrate the PSBT without changing the transaction semantics or tx_id, then \n sends reached_pings_collection and hydrated_psbt to Boomlet.
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert count(reached_pings_collection) == count(peer_ids_collection)
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection contains exactly one \n peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i for each peer_ids_collection[i] [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  peer_i_reached_ping := peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [0 <= i <= \n 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i <= \n 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.ping_seq_num >= latest_seen_ping_seq_num_for_peer_i [0 <= i \n <= 4] \n Assert peer_i_reached_ping.last_seen_block is fresh for current block view [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.reached_mystery_flag == 1 [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection has no missing peers and no duplicate signers
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  hydrated_psbt := hydrate_psbt(psbt)
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert hydrated_psbt.derive_tx_id() == tx_id

' Step 61
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage8 \n reached_pings_collection \n hydrated_psbt
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {reached_pings_collection, hydrated_psbt} from Niso. \n Boomlet independently verifies that every peer has exactly one current reached ping for \n approved_withdrawal_id, \n with current ping sequence, fresh last_seen_block, and reached_mystery_flag set. It then verifies the hydrated \n PSBT preserves the committed tx_id and remains spendable by the Boomerang descriptor before entering signing.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert no pending consent rotation or SAR receipt \n Assert count(reached_pings_collection) == count(peer_ids_collection)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection contains exactly one \n peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i for each peer_ids_collection[i] [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/ping", peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  peer_i_reached_ping := peer_i_reached_ping_signed_by_boomlet_i.content [0 <= i \n <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i \n <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.ping_seq_num >= latest_seen_ping_seq_num_for_peer_i [0 \n <= i <= 4] \n Assert peer_i_reached_ping.last_seen_block is fresh for current block view [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_i_reached_ping.reached_mystery_flag == 1 [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert reached_pings_collection has no missing peers and no duplicate signers
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert hydrated_psbt.derive_tx_id() == tx_id.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert hydrate_psbt(hydrated_psbt) != Null
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert psbt_inputs_match_boomerang_descriptor(hydrated_psbt, boomerang_descriptor) \n == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  psbt := hydrated_psbt.

' Step 62
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage8 \n magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush: Niso receives {magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign"} from Boomlet and proceeds to \n inform User to connect Boomlet to Iso.

' Step 63
Niso o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalNisoOutput1 \n magic: "withdrawal_ready_to_sign_received_connect_boomlet_to_iso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: \n "withdrawal_ready_to_sign_received_connect_boomlet_to_iso"} from Niso and proceeds to connect Boomlet to Iso \n and input \n network, account, key_index, mnemonic, and passphrase to Iso.

' Step 64
User o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalIsoInput1 \n network \n account \n key_index \n mnemonic \n passphrase
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {network, account, key_index, mnemonic, passphrase} from User and \n reconstructs normal_privkey_0 at m/52102'/coin_type'/account'/0/key_index using the same values as setup. \n It derives normal_pubkey_0 and informs Boomlet that MuSig2 signing can start for the PSBT inputs.
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  coin_type := 0 if network is mainnet else 1 \n master_xpriv_0 := derive_master_xpriv(mnemonic, passphrase) \n purpose_xpriv_0 := derive_child_xpriv(master_xpriv_0, 52102, hardened: true) \n coin_xpriv_0 := derive_child_xpriv(purpose_xpriv_0, coin_type, hardened: true) \n account_xpriv_0 := derive_child_xpriv(coin_xpriv_0, account, hardened: true) \n external_xpriv_0 := derive_child_xpriv(account_xpriv_0, 0, hardened: false) \n normal_privkey_0 := derive_child_xpriv(external_xpriv_0, key_index, hardened: false) \n normal_pubkey_0 := derive_public_key(normal_privkey_0)

' Step 65
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalIsoBoomletMessage1 \n magic: "withdrawal_initialized_start_signing"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "withdrawal_initialized_start_signing"} from Iso \n and proceeds to share with it the information necessary for \n signing i.e. psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, alongside his own public nonce \n named pubnonce_boom.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  pubnonce_boom := musig2_generate_pubnonce(psbt, \n boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share) \n signing_package := {psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, pubnonce_boom}

' Step 66
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletIsoMessage1 \n psbt \n boomerang_descriptor \n boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share \n pubnonce_boom
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {psbt, boomerang_descriptor, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, \n pubnonce_boom} from Boomlet. Iso then generates its own public \n nonce and sends this pubnonce_normal alongside his partialsignature (partialsig_normal) to Boomlet.
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  boom_pubkey_0 := derive_musig2_public_key(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, \n normal_pubkey_0) \n pubnonce_normal := musig2_generate_pubnonce(psbt, normal_privkey_0) \n partialsig_normal := musig2_partial_sign(normal_privkey_0, psbt, boomerang_descriptor, pubnonce_normal, \n pubnonce_boom, boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share)
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert psbt_is_internally_consistent(psbt) == True
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert psbt_inputs_match_boomerang_descriptor(psbt, boomerang_descriptor) == True
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert boom_pubkey_0 == descriptor_pubkey_for_peer(boomerang_descriptor, \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey)

' Step 67
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalIsoBoomletMessage2 \n pubnonce_normal \n partialsig_normal
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {pubnonce_normal, partialsig_normal} from Iso, proceeds \n to produce its own partial signature and shares it with Iso. \n Boomlet saves signed psbt on its own memory.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert musig2_verify_partial(normal_pubkey_0, partialsig_normal, psbt, \n pubnonce_normal, pubnonce_boom) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  partialsig_boom := musig2_partial_sign(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share, \n psbt, boomerang_descriptor, pubnonce_boom, pubnonce_normal, normal_pubkey_0) \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0 := musig2_finalize_psbt(psbt, partialsig_normal, partialsig_boom) \n erase MuSig2 nonce material

' Step 68
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletIsoMessage2 \n partialsig_boom
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives partialsig_boom from Boomlet. Iso also keeps signed psbt but \n informs User that he can connect Boomlet to Niso.
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert musig2_verify_partial(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, partialsig_boom, psbt, \n pubnonce_boom, pubnonce_normal) == True
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  psbt_signed_by_peer_0 := musig2_finalize_psbt(psbt, partialsig_normal, \n partialsig_boom) \n erase MuSig2 nonce material

' Step 69
Iso o-> User:  <b>WithdrawalIsoOutput1 \n magic: "withdrawal_psbt_signature_created_connect_boomlet_to_niso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: \n "withdrawal_psbt_signature_created_connect_boomlet_to_niso"} from Iso and proceeds to connect Boomlet to Niso.

' Step 70
User o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalNisoInput2 \n magic: "withdrawal_peer_is_informed_that_boomlet_should_be_connected_to_niso"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {magic: \n "withdrawal_peer_is_informed_that_boomlet_should_be_connected_to_niso"} from User and proceeds to ask Boomlet \n for \n the signed psbt.

' Step 71
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>WithdrawalNisoBoomletMessage9 \n magic: "withdrawal_signing_finished_export_signed_psbt"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "withdrawal_signing_finished_export_signed_psbt"} from Niso and exports psbt_signed_by_peer_0. Boomlet then waits for the final ping's exact SAR receipt and any required backup reset acknowledgment before setting under_duress to false and clearing active withdrawal state and mystery.

' Step 72
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalBoomletNisoMessage9 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender: Boomlet sends a final ping and waits for its exact SAR receipt and any required backup reset acknowledgment. \n under_duress := false \n clear active withdrawal state and mystery
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives psbt_signed_by_peer_0 from Boomlet and forwards it to WT.

' Step 73
Niso o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage5 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_0
autonumber 73 "<b>[00]"

' Step 73 - b
Peers o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNisoWtMessage5 \n psbt_signed_by_peer_i [1 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives psbt_signed_by_peer_0 from Niso and psbt_signed_by_peer_i [1 <= i \n <= 4] from Peers. WT verifies that every signed PSBT fragment belongs to the approved withdrawal transaction, \n aggregates the signed PSBTs, verifies the final transaction tx_id, and relays the resulting tx_signed_by_peers \n to the network.
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert psbt_signed_by_peer_i.derive_tx_id() == tx_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert psbt_signed_by_peer_i belongs to approved_withdrawal_id [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Lavender:  tx_signed_by_peers := aggregate_psbt(psbt_signed_by_peer_i) [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert tx_signed_by_peers.derive_tx_id() == tx_id
hnote over WT #Lavender:  relay_tx(tx_signed_by_peers, network)
end
@endpuml
